Route net/radix.h through LITES's own bsd_malloc wrapper.

include/sys/malloc.h:272 defines

    #define bsd_malloc(size, type, flags) malloc(size)

because the LITES server has a one-argument malloc, not the BSD kernel's
three-argument one. net/radix.h's KERNEL arm was never converted and
still calls malloc and free with BSD arity directly, so the build fails
with

    net/radix.h:133: error: too many arguments to function 'malloc'
    net/radix.h:134: error: too many arguments to function 'free'

Apply with:  patch -p1 -d /path/to/lites < radix-bsd-malloc.patch

--- a/server/net/radix.h
+++ b/server/net/radix.h
@@
-#define R_Malloc(p, t, n) (p = (t) malloc((unsigned long)(n), M_RTABLE, M_DONTWAIT))
-#define Free(p) free((caddr_t)p, M_RTABLE);
+#define R_Malloc(p, t, n) (p = (t) bsd_malloc((unsigned long)(n), M_RTABLE, M_DONTWAIT))
+#define Free(p) bsd_free((caddr_t)p, M_RTABLE);
